Falsifies `system_tests::user::riscv_virtio_tests::a_name_resolves_through_the_stack_and_a_real_one_when_the_host_answers`.

Architecture: riscv64

The defect: `Query::accept` takes every class-IN A record in the answer, not only those owned by
the end of the CNAME chain from the name asked. That is cache poisoning in one line: a reply about
one name plants an address the server gave for another.

Expected to fail: the gating assertion, with client code `0xe14f` (case 4, `poisoned.nife.test`,
a wrong verdict). Measured 2026-10-04 (UTC) on riscv64: red with exactly that code.

diff --git a/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs b/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/domain_name_system/src/lib.rs
@@ -776,7 +776,7 @@
         let mut scan = answers;
         for _ in 0..h.ancount {
             let Ok(record) = scan.record() else { break };
-            if record.class != CLASS_IN || record.rtype != record_type::A || record.name != owner {
+            if record.class != CLASS_IN || record.rtype != record_type::A {
                 continue;
             }
             answer.ttl = answer.ttl.min(believable_time_to_live(record.ttl));
